This is a shell app to address the issue of children using their phones to watch videos on apps like TalkTok and RedNote. Its primary function is similar to Apple iOS's app limits, but I'd like parents to be able to set limits more flexibly, such as requiring children to unlock the app every 10 minutes (e.g., by asking them to answer random questions like traditional Chinese character recognition, math, or English questions). This will essentially encourage children to research and learn. I've currently named it kidsViewer, and its specific features are as follows:
1. Technical Requirements: I'd like to build a cross-platform app based on React, Vite, and Electron (prioritizing iPad, iOS, and Android). I'd support two storage options for system settings (e.g., at least IAPIHandler.ts, LocalAPIHandler.ts, and StandardAPIHandler.ts). The source code directory structure should be divided into multiple directories. The UI color and layout should be aesthetically pleasing and suitable for children's tastes. The underlying framework will use WebViewer or a more advanced web browser to open the short-video URL set by parents. Important: All source code comments should use concise English. Internationalization is supported (including the question bank in the future).
2. Functional Overview: To avoid issues like embedding Douyin/RedNote, Content may be subject to licensing disputes. Parents can set the URL of the short-video platform they wish to access.
2.1 Usage statistics for each person (child) under the parent's (user) account are collected, and daily usage reports are generated for the parent (user). These include usage time, correct/incorrect answer rates, question category preferences, and repeated question accuracy (forgetfulness curve).
3. Operational Procedures:
3.1. Parents: After downloading kidsViewer, the first time you use it, you will need to register your account using your phone number or email address. You will be prompted to set a parental control password. Then, you can add a person (child) by entering a nickname and age range (preschoolers 2-4, younger children 4-6, older children 6-12). You can then set viewing limits (selecting automatic lock after 10m/15m/20m/30m/40m of video viewing, and dynamically randomly prompting N questions within a range (Chinese/Math/English/Other).)
3.2. Children: Upon receiving a parent's configured iPad and watching videos, the app will automatically lock the user according to the pre-set policy and prompt them to answer questions to unlock the user.

